# YAML 1.2
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the SkillPortrait paper and public
  dataset. Replace the placeholder author list below with the canonical author
  block after double-blind review.
title: >-
  SkillPortrait: From Fixed-Suite Benchmarking to Skill-Centered Assessment
authors:
  # FIXME: replace with the real author list before public announcement.
  - name: "Anonymous Authors"
date-released: "2026-07-31"
url: "https://skillaudit.github.io/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SkillAudit/skillaudit"
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21720913
    description: Companion dataset on Zenodo (CDLA-Permissive-2.0).
keywords:
  - large-language-models
  - agent-evaluation
  - skill-assessment
  - benchmark
  - llm-agents
abstract: >-
  SkillPortrait is an evaluation framework that measures the incremental
  task-completion gain that an Anthropic-style /skill markdown file
  provides to a coding or research agent, on top of a baseline run
  without the skill. It pairs scheme generation, sandboxed task
  execution via Harbor, and an LLM judge that scores both utility
  (capability gain) and security (exploitability of skill contents).
  This repository is the open-source companion to the SkillPortrait paper.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  # Replace with the canonical author list after double-blind review.
  authors:
    - name: "Anonymous Authors"
  title: >-
    SkillPortrait: From Fixed-Suite Benchmarking to Skill-Centered Assessment
  year: 2026
  journal: "Preprint"
